  "title": "VEPCON: Source imaging of high-density visual evoked potentials with multi-scale brain parcellations and connectomes",
  "description": "VEPCON is a multimodal BIDS dataset with high-density EEG, structural MRI, and diffusion-weighted imaging from 20 participants. Visual evoked potentials were recorded during face versus scrambled-face discrimination and coherent versus incoherent motion discrimination. Derivatives include preprocessed single-trial EEG, FreeSurfer outputs, multi-scale brain parcellations (83 to 1015 regions), structural connectomes, and EEG source-imaging inverse solutions with code for regional time series.",
  "methods_description": "High-density EEG was recorded during two visual tasks (faces vs. scrambled faces; coherent vs. incoherent motion). MRI and DWI were acquired in a separate session from the same participants. Derivatives were produced with FreeSurfer 7.1.1 and MNE (BEM models), with parcellations at 5 spatial resolutions and connectomes based on fiber count, fiber density, fractional anisotropy, and mean diffusivity.",
